  "answer": "I found no past ticket that reports this Peek problem. That problem is PowerToys.Peek.UI.exe accepting a nonexistent runner PID, such as 9999999, and then running with no UI. The closest tickets are about other modules. PowerToys#41709 covers Awake being left unresponsive when its parent process binding fails. That is a different module, so I don't count it as a match. Treat this as a new bug and keep the report open for the Peek maintainers. Until it's fixed, don't launch PowerToys.Peek.UI.exe by hand with an arbitrary argument. Let PowerToys start Peek. If a stray instance is left running, end it in Task Manager."
 },
